window.STORY6=Object.assign(window.STORY6||{},{
"Goryeo":["In 918 the general Wang Geon founded Goryeo, taking the name of the ancient kingdom Goguryeo, and by 936 reunited the peninsula. The name 'Korea' comes from Goryeo.","Goryeo's artisans made famous jade-green celadon pottery. Monks carved the entire Buddhist canon onto over 81,000 woodblocks, the Tripitaka Koreana, to seek protection from the Mongols; they survive at Haeinsa temple."],
"The Tale of Genji":["Around 1010, Murasaki Shikibu, a lady-in-waiting at the Heian court, wrote The Tale of Genji, following the loves and life of the 'Shining Prince' Genji and then his descendants.","It is often called the world's first novel, and its psychological depth is still admired. Her diary describes court life and her rival, Sei Shōnagon, author of The Pillow Book."],
"The Jade Emperor":["In Chinese folk religion, the Jade Emperor rules heaven like an emperor, with a celestial bureaucracy of gods who report on humans. In 1015 the Song emperor Zhenzong formally gave him imperial titles.","Legend says he chose the animals of the zodiac by a race; the rat won by riding on the ox's back. The Kitchen God reports to him each New Year."],
"Paper money":["Merchants in Sichuan in the early 1000s used paper notes, jiaozi, as receipts for heavy iron coins. In 1024 the Song government took over and issued the first official paper money.","Marco Polo later marvelled at Kublai Khan's paper currency. Overprinting led to inflation in the Yuan and Ming."],
"Compass & clock tower":["In 1088 the scholar Shen Kuo's Dream Pool Essays described a magnetic needle that points south, and noted magnetic declination. Compasses were soon used at sea.","In 1088 Su Song built a 12-metre astronomical clock tower in Kaifeng, powered by a water wheel with an escapement, that rang bells and turned a celestial globe."],
"Water Margin":["Song Jiang led a real band of outlaws in Shandong around 1121, mentioned briefly in Song histories. Over three centuries, storytellers and playwrights turned it into The Water Margin, a 14th-century novel of 108 heroes who gather at the Liangshan Marsh.", "The outlaws, among them the tiger-killing Wu Song and the drunken monk Lu Zhishen, fight corrupt officials in the name of righteousness, then accept an imperial pardon and die fighting for the state. It is one of China's four great classical novels."],
"Jurchens take Kaifeng":["In 1127 the Jurchen Jin dynasty from Manchuria captured the Song capital Kaifeng, taking the retired emperor Huizong, a great painter, and his son captive.","The Song court fled south and rebuilt at Hangzhou. The general Yue Fei, who fought to recover the north, was executed on false charges."],
"Milarepa":["Milarepa, Tibet's most beloved yogi, used black magic as a young man to take revenge on relatives who had cheated his family. Repenting, he studied under the teacher Marpa, who made him build and tear down towers.","He meditated in caves, living on nettles until his skin turned green. His songs of realization are still sung."],
"Genpei War":["From 1180 to 1185, the Minamoto and Taira clans fought for control of Japan. At the sea battle of Dan-no-ura, the Taira were destroyed; the child emperor Antoku drowned.","Minamoto Yoritomo became shogun in 1192, beginning nearly 700 years of samurai rule."],
"Yoshitsune & Benkei":["Minamoto Yoshitsune, Yoritomo's brilliant younger brother, won the Genpei War but was hunted by his jealous brother.","His companion, the giant warrior-monk Benkei, is said to have died standing, full of arrows, defending the gate while Yoshitsune took his own life."],
"The Eight Immortals":["The Eight Immortals of Daoism, a group fixed in Yuan and Ming plays, are ordinary people who gained immortality: among them Lü Dongbin with his demon-slaying sword, the beggar Li Tieguai with his iron crutch and gourd, and He Xiangu, the only woman, with her lotus.", "In the tale 'The Eight Immortals Cross the Sea', each crosses the ocean using a magic tool instead of a cloud, giving a proverb for showing one's own talents. They appear on porcelain, paintings and in Chinese opera."]
});
